msoffice-crypt (1.1+git20260911.b5fed29-noble1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Build from upstream source (commit b5fed29, 2026-09-11) instead of shipping
    a prebuilt x86-64 binary, so Launchpad builds it for amd64 and arm64. This
    upstream version also fixes AES-256 key generation for -encMode 1.
  * Compile against cybozulib 4959b9a (component tarball) so hashing and AES
    still go through OpenSSL, keeping SHA-384 support and CPUs without AES-NI.
  * Depend on the OpenSSL runtime library instead of libssl-dev.

 -- REMnux Distribution <distro@remnux.org>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 23:47:58 -0400

